            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Reminiscent of a country estate, with the convenience of a central location, Ottawa’s oldest wood-frame house is surrounded by approximately eight acres of landscaped greenspace and gardens.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p>Use the&nbsp;<a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/facility-rentals">rental search tool</a>&nbsp;to find an event space that meets your needs.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/facility-rentals/grounds-billings-estate-national-historic-site">Grounds&nbsp;</a></li>
<li><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/facility-rentals/sallys-kitchen-billings-estate-national-historic-site">Sally's Kitchen</a> (multi-purpose room)<br><br>
	Note: Sally’s Kitchen is not a functional kitchen for food preparation; the name reflects the space’s historical use.</li>
<li><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/facility-rentals/farmhands-house-billings-estate-national-historic-site">Farmhand's House</a>&nbsp;(multi-purpose room)</li>
</ul>
<p>For more information, please contact our Customer Service Booking Clerk. Call <strong>613-580-2088</strong> or email <a href="mailto:museums@ottawa.ca">museums@ottawa.ca</a>.</p>
